{% render 'logo-frame-contrast' %}

<div class="sf-join-container">

  {%- if customer == nil -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      GUEST VIEW: SHOW THE STORE, THEN OFFER THE ACCOUNT.

      This used to redirect straight to Shopify account creation. Someone who
      clicked a cold email saw "Redirecting to login..." and never saw a logo,
      a product or a price — while the email that sent them here promised a
      working store they could look at.

      So the invite card renders for guests too, with two doors. Preview needs
      no account and opens the real store read-only. Join is the same flow it
      always was, taken by someone who has now seen what they are joining.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Preview always has a door. Stores that carry a join_code use it as the
      token; stores without one accept ?preview=1, because their join link
      already lets any holder become a member — looking is less than that.
      Gating the button on a code most stores do not have is exactly why it
      failed to render at all.
    {%- endcomment -%}
